  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Investigate whether a syntactic guarded modality (a <html:em>later</html:em> modality
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\blacktriangleright ]]></fr:tex>) can be added to the dependent Lambek calculus to
internalize well-founded recursion.</html:p>
    <html:p>The key question is whether the linear/ordered structure of the Lambek
calculus places constraints on how the modality interacts with the tensor and
hom types — and whether guardedness can still enforce productivity/termination
in this setting.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
